From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:23:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/22] gtk: a touch taps and scrolls where the finger touched

GTK moves no pointer for a touch, so the cursor stayed where the mouse
last was: a touch drag scrolled there (the HOTTY document under the mouse,
or the mouse report's position), and a tap clicked there. The touch's
start point is now the cursor's when it begins and while it scrolls, so
mouseButtonCallback and scrollCallback see where the finger is.

Generic, in upstream's style, a fix to "gtk: a touch drag scrolls".
Upstream lines: 15 (GTK apprt only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig b/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig
index 0ab68fe8d..3f7b22ead 100644
--- a/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig
+++ b/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig
@@ -669,6 +669,10 @@ pub const Surface = extern struct {
         touch_scroll_x: f64 = 0,
         touch_scroll_y: f64 = 0,
 
+        /// Where the live touch began, in surface pixels: its taps and its
+        /// scroll happen there, not where the mouse pointer was.
+        touch_start: apprt.CursorPos = .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 },
+
         /// True when the child has exited.
         child_exited: bool = false,
 
@@ -3058,13 +3062,19 @@ pub const Surface = extern struct {
     // The gesture is touch-only, so a mouse drag still selects text.
     fn touchScrollBegin(
         _: *gtk.GestureDrag,
-        _: f64,
-        _: f64,
+        start_x: f64,
+        start_y: f64,
         self: *Self,
     ) callconv(.c) void {
         const priv = self.private();
         priv.touch_scroll_x = 0;
         priv.touch_scroll_y = 0;
+        // GTK moves no pointer for a touch, so the cursor would stay where
+        // the mouse last was: the touch's point is the cursor's, for its tap
+        // (mouseButtonCallback) and its scroll (scrollCallback).
+        const start = self.scaledCoordinates(start_x, start_y);
+        priv.touch_start = .{ .x = @floatCast(start.x), .y = @floatCast(start.y) };
+        priv.cursor_pos = priv.touch_start;
     }
 
     fn touchScrollUpdate(
@@ -3081,6 +3091,9 @@ pub const Surface = extern struct {
 
         const core_surface = priv.core_surface orelse return;
         const scaled = self.scaledCoordinates(dx, dy);
+        // The scroll happens where the finger touched, as a touchpad's does
+        // where the pointer is.
+        priv.cursor_pos = priv.touch_start;
         // GestureDrag is in screen pixels with y down: a finger up (negative
         // y) moves the content up, a scroll down — what a natural-scrolling
         // touchpad does. EcMouseScrollVertical inverts GTK's touchpad deltas
